{#
================================================================================
[NOTES]
================================================================================
Prompt: wave_chapter.j2
Service Step: WAVE_CHAPTER (long-form scene-weaving, Generate phase Step 2 in the long-form 6-stage architecture)
Function Summary:
  This step **singles** weaves multiple scene drafts into a complete long-form chapter after DRAFT completes all scenes.
  Core Responsibilities:
    1. Add transitional paragraphs or sentences between scenes
    2. Fulfill plan.cross_scene_intent.cross_scene_references (callback/foreshadow/parallel/contrast/echo)
    3. Adjust local pacing according to plan.cross_scene_intent.pacing_curve
    4. Unify cross-scene POV, voice, and style
    5. Remove cross-scene repetitions or supplement anchors when needed
  Strictly Prohibited:
    - Rewriting any scene's POV main body in full paragraphs
    - Deleting entire scenes
    - Adding new scenes
    - Modifying locked POV characters in plan.scene_intents
    - Word count exceeding +/-30% from target
Upstream Input:
  - draft_text: Current chapter draft output from DRAFT phase
  - stage_cards.source: ChapterSourceSlice, containingthis chapter's forbidden revelation boundaries and voice/style projections
  - stage_cards: Local derived cards for plan / characters / editorial / style / quality
  - cross_scene_intent: Cross-scene constraints from plan (2 fields: cross_scene_references + pacing_curve)
Downstream Output:
  - TEXT: Woven complete chapter body
Consumption Chain Priority:
  P0 = Smooth inter-scene transitions / Cross-scene reference hits / POV consistency / Word count within +/-30%
  P1 = pacing_curve rhythm matching / Motif continuity as soft reference only, no hard supplements for responses / Character voice cross-scene consistency
  P2 = Style capsules / Serial-read engagement capsules
================================================================================
#}

